BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:khoj-mozilla-counterstructures-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151909Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Khoj x Mozilla Foundation: Counterstructures Residency 20
 26 (Delhi)
DESCRIPTION:Counterstructures is Mozilla Foundation's cultural R&D residenc
 y\, in which creative technologists prototype alternatives to dominant tec
 h systems: cultural artifacts\, installations and tools that question and 
 reframe them. Each edition operationalises the findings of a regional part
 icipatory assembly into thematic tracks\; the Delhi edition\, hosted by Kh
 oj International Artists' Association\, works from Mozilla's assemblies wi
 th G5A in Delhi and Mumbai and runs on two tracks. RETAINING CULTURAL AUTH
 ORITY asks what happens when oral\, embodied or community-held knowledge i
 s converted into datasets and machine-readable forms\, which cultural mate
 rials become visible to AI systems and which do not\, and how communities 
 can retain authority over what is digitised\, interpreted\, reused or deli
 berately kept private. REMEMBERING AND THINKING WITH MACHINES asks where t
 hought resides when people think with machines\, at what stage human judgm
 ent enters the system\, and what cultural or professional knowledge is los
 t when judgment is standardised through automation. Proposals may respond 
 to one or both tracks and can take many forms\, but must critically counte
 r the questions the tracks raise rather than simply illustrate them. WHAT 
 RESIDENTS DO: prototype an artifact\, installation\, system\, artwork or t
 ool for public exhibition\; take part in listening\, reading\, workshops a
 nd facilitated critique\, testing ideas with peers and community members\;
  write a 750-word report on the project's development and insights for the
  Counterstructures report and online archive\; and present the work public
 ly. WHO IT IS FOR: creative technologists and multidisciplinary artists us
 ing technology as a medium for cultural inquiry\, bringing critical perspe
 ctives and research-driven practice. Experience with AI can be early-stage
  or advanced\, but SOME PROFICIENCY WITH CODING IS REQUIRED. ELIGIBILITY: 
 this Delhi edition is open to Indian nationals only. Earlier editions ran 
 with tiat in San Francisco (responding to Hollywood's 8 Rules for AI) and 
 with Rhizome in New York\, whose residents showed at the New Museum. APPLY
  through the Mozilla Foundation form at https://mozillafoundation.tfaforms
 .net/f/khojresidency\; the guiding principles for the call are set out in 
 the form. Deadline 13 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Khoj International 
 Artists' Association in collaboration with Mozilla Foundation\nLocation: N
 ew Delhi\, India. Weekly in-person sessions at Khoj. INDIAN NATIONALS ONLY
 .\nAward: Mozilla's Creative Futures: Counterstructures programme publishe
 s USD 2\,500 per resident (USD 2\,000 stipend plus a USD 500 materials bud
 get)\, along with weekly in-person work sessions\, guest lectures from pra
 ctitioners across art\, technology and community design\, and publication 
 of the finished project in the collective documentation report. CAVEAT: ne
 ither the Khoj call page nor the Mozilla application form restates a figur
 e for this six-week Delhi edition\, and the published package covers the t
 en-week format\, so confirm the amount with Khoj before applying. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: Six weeks\, 1 October to 12 November 2026\, running
  weekly in Delhi\, with final projects presented publicly 13 to 15 Novembe
 r 2026.\n\nMore: https://khojstudios.org/opportunity/open-call-counterstru
 ctures-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://khojstudios.org/opportunity/open-call-counterstructures-residen
 cy/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India. Weekly in-person sessions at Khoj. INDIAN NATIO
 NALS ONLY.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inlaks-fine-art-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151909Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation: Inlaks Fine Art Award 2027
DESCRIPTION:A one-year award enabling an emerging Indian visual artist to p
 ursue independent practice\, with a stipulation to attend a recognised art
  residency programme in India for four weeks during the year. ELIGIBILITY 
 IS RESTRICTED: Indian citizens currently living in India\, born on or afte
 r 1 January 1996\, who are either recent graduates\, postgraduates or fina
 l-year students of a leading Indian visual arts institute\, or artists wit
 hout those formal credentials but with a record of exhibition participatio
 n. First-year MA students are not eligible. Awardees submit progress repor
 ts at six months and on completion\, plus documentation of the residency. 
 Applications close 15 August 2026 at 23:59 IST via Submittable. Shortlisti
 ng is expected in late October 2026 with interviews in early November.\n\n
 Organisation: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation\nLocation: India. Open to India
 n citizens currently living in India.\nAward: INR 300\,000 (around USD 3\,
 400 / EUR 2\,950) for one year\, plus a fully covered four-week art reside
 ncy at an Indian art institution. No application fee.\nDuration: Twelve mo
 nths of independent practice\, including a mandatory four-week residency w
 ithin India.\n\nMore: https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e1
 4093-df9b-41c5-af96-ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e14093-df9b-41c5-af96
 -ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India. Open to Indian citizens currently living in India.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-inside-out-art-museum-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151909Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Inside-Out Art Museum Residency 2027 (Bei
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at Inside-Out Art Museu
 m (IOAM) in Beijing\, one of China's leading independent platforms for con
 temporary art and research. The museum combines exhibitions\, critical inq
 uiry and public programmes\, giving residents room for in-depth research\,
  experimentation and exchange within a Chinese art scene that is otherwise
  hard to access from Europe. The residency is framed as cultural exchange 
 rather than production to deadline: IOAM works with a flexible model that 
 takes the resident's other obligations into account and sets the exact sta
 rt date in consultation with the selected candidate. WHO: visual artists\,
  curators and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of th
 e Kingdom. Duos and collaborations may apply (two artists\, two curators/c
 ritics\, or a combination who structurally make work together\, submitting
  a joint plan for the work period that leads to a single result\, and who 
 live and work together in the same space during the residency)\, but each 
 individual must submit a separate application\; the apartment is well suit
 ed to duos or partnerships. WORK PERIOD: one period of three months\, 1 Ma
 rch to 30 May 2027\, with room for one artist or duo\; you can state a pre
 ference for the work period in the application form. Selection is by advis
 ory committee\; read the Mondriaan Fund Residency explanation for the cond
 itions\, assessment and checklist\, plus the fund's general terms and cond
 itions\, before applying. DEADLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00
  Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Insi
 de-Out Art Museum\nLocation: Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curator
 s and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdo
 m\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subsidy of EUR 8\,478 for an art
 ist or EUR 5\,622 for a curator/critic toward travel\, material and living
  costs (a 10 percent personal contribution is automatically deducted by th
 e Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living space and Inside-Out Art Museum suppor
 t are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. For a selected duo the total is
  increased proportionally to cover the second applicant's travel and accom
 modation. Contribution for Caribbean-based residents can be increased for 
 higher travel costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 1 March 
 to 30 May 2027 (flexible start date\, set by IOAM in consultation with the
  resident)\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regel
 ingen/residency/inside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regelingen/residency/i
 nside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curators and critics based i
 n the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mon
 driaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:grandtek-core-echo-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151909Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Core Echo 2027: International Open Call & 3-Week Residenc
 y
DESCRIPTION:Core Echo 2027 is an international open call from Grandtek Art 
 Center for a three-week on-site artist residency. SUPPORT PACKAGE: each se
 lected artist receives an initial stipend of RMB 20\,000\, with round-trip
  travel\, accommodation\, and daily meals provided during the on-site resi
 dency. One piece from each artist's exhibited series will enter the perman
 ent collection of the partner enterprise\, with terms specified in a contr
 act signed by the end of the on-site residency period. Dedicated co-creati
 on studios are provided\, and selected partner enterprises offer supplemen
 tary temporary creation zones\; spatial requirements requested by artists 
 will be met to the fullest extent possible. Weekly artist salons are held 
 during the residency for peer exchange and exhibition planning. The call i
 s announced via the organizer's WeChat channel\; check the source for full
  details and the application form. Deadline: 15 July 2026\, 15:59 UTC.\n\n
 Organisation: Grandtek Art Center\nLocation: On-site residency\, likely in
  China (organizer uses WeChat\, stipend in RMB\, and works enter a partner
  enterprise's collection\; exact city not stated in the call). Internation
 al open call.\nAward: Initial stipend of RMB 20\,000 per selected artist. 
 Round-trip travel\, accommodation\, and daily meals provided during the on
 -site residency. Dedicated co-creation studios provided (with supplementar
 y temporary creation zones from partner enterprises). One piece from each 
 artist's exhibited series enters the permanent collection of the partner e
 nterprise\, per a contract signed by the end of the residency.\nDuration: 
 Three-week on-site residency.\n\nMore: https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/etfAYPm1
 ixqdx-iOFWDIwA?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/etfAYPm1ixqdx-iOFWDIwA?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:On-site residency\, likely in China (organizer uses WeChat\, stipe
 nd in RMB\, and works enter a partner enterprise's collection\; exact city
  not stated in the call). International open call.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kyoto-retreat-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151909Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260717
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260718
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Kyoto Retreat 2026
DESCRIPTION:Four-week residency in Kyoto for artists\, curators and writers
  from anywhere in the world\, working in drawing\, painting\, sculpture\, 
 photography\, film\, video\, new media\, installation\, fiction and nonfic
 tion writing\, poetry\, interdisciplinary or social practice. Open to all 
 career stages\, 21 and over. Selected participants notified by 1 September
  2026.\n\nOrganisation: The Kyoto Retreat (founded by Dexter Wimberly)\nLo
 cation: Kyoto\, Japan\nAward: Roundtrip flight\, private accommodation and
  $800 USD stipend\nDuration: 4 weeks (1 to 30 November 2026)\n\nMore: http
 s://www.kyotoretreat.com?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.kyotoretreat.com?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
LOCATION:Kyoto\, Japan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nakanojo-biennale-2027-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151909Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260712
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260713
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nakanojo Biennale 2027: International Artist Open Call (G
 unma Prefecture\, Japan)
DESCRIPTION:Nakanojo Biennale 2027 (11th edition) is an international open 
 call for artists of all genres — sculpture\, painting\, photography\, vi
 deo art\, installation\, performance\, and more — to exhibit in Nakanojo
  Town\, Gunma Prefecture\, Japan. Theme: 'Echoing Green'\, inspired by Wil
 liam Blake's poem\, exploring cycles of life\, regeneration\, and connecti
 on between past and future generations. Open internationally to individual
  artists and artist groups at all career stages\; new participants are enc
 ouraged. A production grant is provided (amount not publicly specified)\; 
 no exhibition or residency fees are charged. Residency accommodation avail
 able from April 2027. Staff support provided for venue selection and insta
 llation guidance. First-time participants in Japan must attend an on-site 
 venue inspection\; an online orientation on 5 September 2026 is required f
 or all accepted artists. Deadline: 12 July 2026 at 23:59 JST (online). App
 ly via Google Form at https://forms.gle/SS8DaaGA6uwUKogj7. Full details at
  https://nakanojo-biennale.com/2027-open-call/english.html. Contact: offic
 e@nakanojo-biennale.com.\n\nOrganisation: Nakanojo Biennale Executive Comm
 ittee / Nakanojo Town\, Gunma Prefecture\nLocation: Nakanojo Town\, Gunma 
 Prefecture\, Japan\nAward: Production grant provided (amount not specified
  publicly). No exhibition fee\, no residency fee. Insurance subsidies avai
 lable. Artists responsible for materials\, food\, transportation\, and ins
 tallation/removal costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Exhibition: 18 Sep
 tember – 24 October 2027 (37 days). Production period: April–August 20
 27. Residency accommodation available from April 2027.\n\nMore: https://na
 kanojo-biennale.com/2027-open-call/english.html?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nakanojo-biennale.com/2027-open-call/english.html?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nakanojo Town\, Gunma Prefecture\, Japan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-arko-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151909Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x ARKO Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Third edition of transmediale's residency in collaboration with
  Arts Council Korea (ARKO)\, awarded to one person of Korean nationality (
 based in Korea or elsewhere) working in digital art and moving image pract
 ices\, design\, sound and media theory. Open to artists\, researchers\, pr
 actitioners\, designers and sound artists across all formats. The two-mont
 h residency comes with an artist fee of EUR 1\,500 per month\, additional 
 production support\, and travel and accommodation support for the festival
  and residency\; duos and collectives are welcome but share the same fee. 
 Part of transmediale's 2027 programme (40th anniversary\, themed 'RFC 40')
 \, which seeks proposals offering alternatives to how we understand\, resp
 ond to and shape our technological conditions\, moving from critique to co
 nstruction outside extractive logics. Deadline: 28 August 2026\, 23:59 CES
 T.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with Arts Council Korea /
  ARKO)\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany (two-month residency around the transme
 diale festival)\; applicants must be of Korean nationality (based in Korea
  or elsewhere)\nAward: Two-month residency with an artist fee of EUR 1\,50
 0 per month\, additional production support\, plus travel and accommodatio
 n support for the festival and residency. For duos or collectives the fee 
 remains the same and is shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month r
 esidency\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/transmediale-x-arko-resi
 dency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/transmediale-x-arko-residency?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany (two-month residency around the transmediale fest
 ival)\; applicants must be of Korean nationality (based in Korea or elsewh
 ere)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:making-space-guangzhou-nl-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151909Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
SUMMARY:Deadline: Making Space Residency 2027 for Netherlands-Based Practit
 ioners (Guangzhou)
DESCRIPTION:The Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands in China\, in par
 tnership with artist-run space Making Space in Guangzhou\, invites Netherl
 ands-based artists\, makers\, curators\, writers\, researchers and other c
 ultural practitioners to a six-week residency in spring 2027. Making Space
  (est. 2017) focuses on art and social practice with an emphasis on long-t
 erm research\, local knowledge and care-driven collaboration. The residenc
 y is process-oriented with no obligation to produce finished work\; the re
 sident takes part in at least one public exchange (talk\, workshop\, readi
 ng group\, screening\, performance or open studio). SUPPORT: EUR 2\,700 tr
 avel and artist fee subsidy (fixed per application\; duos or collectives s
 hare the amount)\, accommodation in Guangzhou\, shared studio space\, cura
 torial and research support with access to local networks\, and logistical
  support for public programming (extra funding may be considered for publi
 c programmes). The resident arranges their own China visa\; Making Space p
 rovides an invitation letter. LOOKING FOR: practitioners engaging with alt
 ernative education\, ecological justice\, migration and labour\, social pr
 actice\, intergenerational narratives\, diaspora and transdisciplinary col
 laboration\; English communication required. APPLY by email (makingspace20
 17@gmail.com) with a 200-word bio\, CV\, 2-page project proposal and portf
 olio (max 20 pages) in a single PDF\, in English. Result expected late Nov
 ember 2026. Deadline: 3 October 2026\, 23:59 CST / 17:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Making Space\, in partnership with the Embassy of the Kingdom of the
  Netherlands in China\nLocation: Guangzhou\, China\nAward: EUR 2\,700 trav
 el and artist fee subsidy (fixed per application\; duos or collectives sha
 re it)\, plus accommodation in Guangzhou and shared studio space\nDuration
 : Six continuous weeks between 15 March and 15 June 2027\, dates agreed wi
 th the selected resident\n\nMore: https://makingspace2017.notion.site/open
 -call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://makingspace2017.notion.site/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Guangzhou\, China
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
